    prompt: `Create a comprehensive web performance optimization plan:\n\nAudit Phase:\n- Run Lighthouse on mobile and desktop\n- Analyze Core Web Vitals (LCP, INP, CLS) in Chrome UX Report\n- Generate a waterfall chart from WebPageTest\n- Identify render-blocking resources\n- Check for unused JavaScript and CSS (Coverage tab)\n- Audit third-party scripts and their impact\n\nOptimization checklist:\n1. JavaScript:\n   - Code splitting with dynamic imports (route-level and component-level)\n   - Tree shaking verification (check bundle analyzer output)\n   - Defer non-critical scripts (async/defer attributes)\n   - Remove unused polyfills (use @babel/preset-env with browserslist)\n   - Implement virtual scrolling for long lists\n   - Web Worker offloading for heavy computation\n\n2. CSS:\n   - Inline critical CSS in <head>\n   - Remove unused CSS (PurgeCSS)\n   - Minify and compress (Brotli level 11 for static assets)\n   - Use CSS containment (contain: layout style paint) on off-screen elements\n   - Font loading strategy: font-display: swap, subset fonts, preload\n\n3. Images:\n   - Responsive images with srcset and sizes\n   - Next-gen formats (WebP/AVIF) with <picture> fallback\n   - Lazy loading (loading=\"lazy\" + Intersection Observer for background images)\n   - Proper dimensions to prevent CLS (width/height attributes or aspect-ratio)\n   - Use CDN with image optimization (imgix, Cloudinary, or Cloudflare Images)\n\n4. Network:\n   - HTTP/2 or HTTP/3 with multiplexing\n   - Resource hints: preconnect, dns-prefetch for third-party origins\n   - Preload key resources (fonts, hero image, critical JS/CSS)\n   - Prefetch likely next pages\n   - Service Worker for caching and offline support\n   - CDN configuration with proper cache headers\n\n5. Rendering:\n   - Avoid layout thrashing (batch DOM reads and writes)\n   - Use will-change and transform for animations (GPU acceleration)\n   - Implement content-visibility: auto for below-fold content\n   - Reduce DOM size (<1500 nodes target)\n\nProvide a monitoring setup (Lighthouse CI, Web Vitals JS library) and a before/after comparison template.`,
