    description: "Write a persuasive customer success story that demonstrates value and drives conversions.",
    prompt: `Write a customer case study for [Customer Name] using [Your Product/Service]:\n\nStructure:\n\n1. Executive Summary Box (hero section):\n- [Customer Name] achieved [key metric] improvement using [Product]\n- 3-5 key results in large font, visually prominent:\n  - Result 1: "XX% increase in [metric]"\n  - Result 2: "XX hours saved per week"\n  - Result 3: "$XXX in cost savings"\n\n2. About the Customer (50-75 words):\n- Industry, company size, location\n- Their role and team size\n- What they were trying to accomplish\n\n3. The Challenge (100-150 words):\n- What was the situation before using your product?\n- What specific pain points were they experiencing?\n- What solutions had they tried that didn't work?\n- Quote from the customer about their frustration (verbatim, with permission)\n\n4. The Solution (100-150 words):\n- How did they discover your product?\n- What was the implementation process like?\n- Which specific features did they use?\n- Quote about the onboarding/implementation experience\n\n5. The Results (150-200 words):\n- Before vs. after comparison (use a comparison table if comparing metrics)\n- Quantitative results with timeframes ("within 3 months")\n- Qualitative benefits (team morale, customer satisfaction, competitive advantage)\n- Unexpected benefits they discovered\n- Quote about the impact ("This changed how we...)\n\n6. The Future (50 words):\n- What's next for this customer?\n- How will they expand their use of your product?\n\n7. Call to Action:\n- "See how [Product] can help your team achieve similar results"\n- Link to demo, trial, or sales call\n\nDesign notes:\n- Customer photo or company logo (with permission)\n- Pull quotes in large, styled text throughout\n- Results section visually distinct (colored background, large numbers)\n- 1-2 screenshots of the product in use (with customer data blurred if needed)\n\nInterview question guide (to gather this information from the customer):\n- 10-15 questions that will yield the content above\n- Include "What would you tell someone considering [Product]?" for the endorsement quote`,
