    prompt: `Design an executive analytics dashboard for [company type]:\n\nDesign Principles:\n- One screen, no scrolling (everything must be visible at a glance)\n- Information hierarchy: most important top-left (F-pattern reading)\n- Each metric answers "Are we winning?" — not "Here's some data"\n- Trends + context (vs. target, vs. last period, vs. forecast)\n- Actionable: executives should know what to DO after viewing\n\nLayout (6-zone dashboard):\n\nZone 1 — North Star Metric (top-left, largest):\n- The one metric that defines success (revenue, DAU, GMV, NPS)\n- Display: big number + sparkline (30-day trend) + % vs. target\n- Drill-down: click to see by region/product/channel\n\nZone 2 — KPI Tiles (top row, 4-6 tiles):\n- Supporting metrics that drive the north star\n- Each tile: metric name, value, sparkline, % change vs. prior period\n- Color coding: green (ahead of target), yellow (within 5%), red (off track)\n- Examples: MRR, Churn Rate, CAC, LTV, Gross Margin, Active Users\n\nZone 3 — Trend Chart (middle-left, 2/3 width):\n- Time-series chart of primary metric\n- Show: actual line, target line, forecast line (dashed)\n- Time range toggle: 30d / 90d / YTD / 12M\n- Annotations: mark key events (launches, holidays, incidents)\n\nZone 4 — Breakdown (middle-right, 1/3 width):\n- Dimension breakdown of primary metric (by region, product, channel)\n- Horizontal bar chart (sorted by value)\n- Click a bar to filter entire dashboard\n\nZone 5 — Leading Indicators (bottom-left, 1/2 width):\n- Forward-looking metrics that predict future performance\n- Pipeline coverage, trial starts, feature adoption, support tickets\n- Early warning signals: color changes when metrics trend negatively\n\nZone 6 — Actions & Insights (bottom-right, 1/2 width):\n- Automated insights: "Revenue dropped 15% in West region — correlated with X"\n- Anomaly detection alerts: "Unusual: churn spiked yesterday"\n- Recommended actions based on data patterns\n\nInteractivity:\n- Global date range selector with comparison period toggle\n- All charts linked: clicking a region filters all charts\n- Export: PDF for board meetings, CSV for analysis\n- Scheduled email: daily/weekly snapshot delivered to inbox\n\nData Requirements:\n- Refresh frequency (real-time, hourly, daily)\n- Data sources and transformation logic\n- SLA: data available by 9am daily\n\nProvide dashboard layout mockup description, SQL queries for key metrics, and implementation plan.`,
