    title: "Business Plan Template",
    description: "Write a comprehensive business plan covering strategy, operations, financials, and growth roadmap.",
    prompt: `Write a business plan for [Company Name]:\n\n1. Executive Summary (1 page):\n- What: One-sentence description of the business\n- Problem: The pain point you solve\n- Solution: How you solve it differently/better\n- Market: Size and growth rate of addressable market\n- Traction: Revenue, users, partnerships to date\n- Team: Why this team can execute\n- Ask: What you need (funding, partnership, hiring)\n\n2. Company Description:\n- Mission statement\n- Legal structure (LLC, C-Corp, etc.) and ownership\n- Company history and key milestones\n- Current status and stage\n\n3. Market Analysis:\n- Industry overview and trends\n- TAM, SAM, SOM with methodology and sources\n- Target customer segments with detailed personas\n- Competitive landscape:\n  - Direct competitors (same solution)\n  - Indirect competitors (different solution, same problem)\n  - Substitutes (manual workarounds, Excel, doing nothing)\n  - Competitive advantage matrix (features × competitors)\n- Barriers to entry for new competitors\n\n4. Product / Service:\n- Core product description with screenshots/mockups\n- Key features and benefits (not just features — why they matter)\n- Development roadmap (next 6-12 months)\n- Intellectual property (patents, trademarks, trade secrets)\n- Technology stack and infrastructure\n\n5. Marketing & Sales Strategy:\n- Go-to-market strategy (see GTM prompt for details)\n- Customer acquisition channels and estimated CAC per channel\n- Sales process and cycle length\n- Partnerships and distribution channels\n- Brand and positioning strategy\n\n6. Operations Plan:\n- Key processes and workflows\n- Suppliers, vendors, and dependencies\n- Facilities and equipment needs\n- Technology and tools\n- Customer support and success processes\n- Quality control and compliance\n\n7. Management Team:\n- Founders and key team members with bios\n- Advisory board or mentors\n- Key hires needed in next 12 months\n- Organizational chart\n- Equity and compensation structure\n\n8. Financial Plan (3-5 year projections):\n- Revenue model and pricing\n- Revenue projections (monthly for year 1, quarterly for years 2-3, annually for years 4-5)\n- Cost structure:\n  - Fixed costs (salaries, rent, tools)\n  - Variable costs (hosting, payment processing, customer support per user)\n  - CAC and LTV calculations\n- Break-even analysis\n- Cash flow statement\n- Balance sheet\n- Key assumptions and risks\n- Scenarios: base case, upside case, downside case\n\n9. Funding Request (if applicable):\n- Amount sought and instrument (equity, convertible note, SAFE, loan)\n- Use of funds breakdown (hiring, marketing, product, runway)\n- Milestones this funding will achieve\n- Future funding rounds anticipated\n\n10. Appendix:\n- Detailed financial spreadsheets\n- Market research data and sources\n- Product screenshots/mockups\n- Customer testimonials and case studies\n- Letters of intent from partners or customers\n- Resumes of key team members\n\nFormat: Professional document, 15-25 pages. Clear headings, charts for financials, consistent formatting.`,
